WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.760
Star-studded casts, pandemic nightmares,&nbsp;
and a puppet that cost more than a mansion:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.315
Can TV shows possibly get&nbsp;
more expensive than this?

00:00:09.315 --> 00:00:14.280
Taking the grand prize for the most expensive&nbsp;
television production to date is The Lord of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:19.740
the Rings: The Rings of Power, which came&nbsp;
in at a whopping $58 million per episode.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:25.260
An epic high fantasy series based on the world&nbsp;
of J. R. R. Tolkien, The Rings of Power takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:29.640
place millennia before the events of The Hobbit&nbsp;
and The Lord of the Rings. When the rights to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:35.100
a Tolkien TV series first went up for grabs, a&nbsp;
bidding war erupted between major streamers HBO,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:41.820
Amazon, and Netflix, with Amazon beating out&nbsp;
its rivals with a hefty bid of $250 million.

00:00:42.095 --> 00:00:44.820
"This could be the beginning of a new era."

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:50.580
In a world of AR sound stages and green screens,&nbsp;
The Rings of Power stands out for its elaborate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:55.800
sets and on-location shoots, which production&nbsp;
designer Ramsey Avery says are meant to capture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:00.480
the golden age of Middle-Earth, long before&nbsp;
Sauron's villainous shenanigans start to drag&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:05.220
everything down. Factor in the elaborate&nbsp;
costumes and full-scale ensemble cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:09.180
and you've got a recipe for the&nbsp;
priciest series ever made — in fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:13.320
with a grand total of five seasons ordered&nbsp;
and already planned in their entirety,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:17.134
the show's total budget could come&nbsp;
in at more than a billion dollars.

00:01:17.134 --> 00:01:20.280
At a time when Netflix has been&nbsp;
tightening its purse strings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:25.320
one show that the platform has funneled endless&nbsp;
money into is the hit supernatural sci-fi series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:29.820
Stranger Things. Since the show's $6&nbsp;
million per episode freshman season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:34.560
Netflix has gradually increased its&nbsp;
budget while continuing to ramp up the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:39.060
killer computer-generated and practical&nbsp;
effects. Not only that, but, by 2018,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:45.720
several of the show's cast were taking home&nbsp;
paychecks of around $250K–$350K per episode.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:51.300
It's estimated that the price tag for the fourth&nbsp;
season came in at around $30 million per episode.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:54.360
According to Netflix executive Ted Sarandos,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:58.380
a hefty chunk of Season 4's spending&nbsp;
increase can be attributed to COVID,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:03.960
which, between the need for extra protocols and&nbsp;
production shutdowns, hit the budget hard. Still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:09.000
it was money well spent. The show features&nbsp;
some of the most beautiful CGI out there and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:14.160
is a testament to the truly cinematic quality&nbsp;
a well-executed streaming series can have. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:20.000
attention to detail even earned Stranger Things&nbsp;
the Emmy for best prosthetic makeup in 2022.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:26.220
The second prequel to Taylor Sheridan's hit&nbsp;
series Yellowstone, 1923 follows the Dutton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:30.900
family during the tumultuous years leading&nbsp;
up to the Great Depression. Comparing his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:34.980
latest show to Lawrence of Arabia in&nbsp;
terms of scale, Sheridan told Deadline:

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:37.560
"I don't know what the Game&nbsp;
of Thrones budgets were,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:39.900
but I don't know how they could&nbsp;
have been more than this."

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:45.780
One of the show's big-ticket items is its cast, an&nbsp;
ensemble led by Hollywood legends Helen Mirren and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:50.760
Harrison Ford — but this is just the beginning.&nbsp;
To create the sense of life on a Montana ranch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:56.520
the series uses thousands of real cattle&nbsp;
and sheep. And much of 1923 was filmed in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:02.760
a span of overseas locations, including&nbsp;
Malta, Tanzania, Kenya, and South Africa.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:08.340
Filming during the pandemic also meant that COVID&nbsp;
protocols upped the budget even further. Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:12.360
of course, you've got the added cost of&nbsp;
a historical series — it's no mean feat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:16.440
to build and dress sets for a show set&nbsp;
100 years in the past. The grand total&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:21.360
for this gorgeously rendered drama comes&nbsp;
in at around $30 million per episode.

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:30.000
"It's time. Alright, okay? Let's give 'em hell."

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:36.540
The MCU Disney+ series Hawkeye racked up a $150&nbsp;
million price tag during its six-episode run,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:42.360
which comes out at around $25 million per episode.&nbsp;
For the sake of comparison, Captain Marvel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:48.780
one of Marvel's theatrical releases, boasted a&nbsp;
budget of around $152 million. As with many other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:54.000
big-budget TV shows, one of Hawkeye's major&nbsp;
costs was its star power: Jeremy Renner, who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:58.680
reprises his role as the titular Avenger, is one&nbsp;
of the higher-paid actors in the Marvel universe.

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:03.660
While his salary for the series isn't widely&nbsp;
known, Parade reported that the actor made $15&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:09.960
million for Avengers: Endgame and likely took home&nbsp;
a similar paycheck for Hawkeye. As the series was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:14.940
primarily filmed in New York City, Georgia, and&nbsp;
Ontario, they weren't exactly dropping much of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:19.680
the budget on hauling an entire cast and crew&nbsp;
from one exotic location to the next. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:25.140
as is the case with many MCU shows and movies,&nbsp;
Hawkeye will have required a significant amount&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:30.420
of CGI, which always ramps up the budget. Judging&nbsp;
by the controversy stemming from the disappointing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:35.580
effects in Episode 3, however, as well as greater&nbsp;
complaints about pay and working conditions from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:41.228
Marvel VFX teams, it seems that this is one area&nbsp;
in which the franchise shouldn't be cutting costs.

00:04:41.228 --> 00:04:46.468
As the first Marvel series to be released on&nbsp;
Disney+, and the first of the MCU's Phase Four,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.468 --> 00:04:51.420
WandaVision was a much-hyped and well-received&nbsp;
entry into the Marvel canon. Like the comics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:56.880
themselves, the MCU keeps things fresh by serving&nbsp;
up a variety of genres and storytelling styles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:01.500
and WandaVision is a stunning example&nbsp;
of this. Starring Elizabeth Olsen as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:05.160
Wanda Maximoff and Paul Bettany as&nbsp;
Vision, the series finds the pair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:08.940
trapped in a strange alternate reality&nbsp;
that looks and feels like a laugh-track&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:13.440
sitcom. As the episodes progress, the pair&nbsp;
transitions from one decade to the next,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:18.240
traveling through sets inspired by some of&nbsp;
the 20th century's most beloved TV shows.

00:05:18.494 --> 00:05:22.574
"We are an unusual couple, you know."
"Oh, I don't think that was ever in question"

00:05:23.468 --> 00:05:28.680
Like other Marvel shows, WandaVision was given&nbsp;
a generous budget of about $25 million per&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:34.440
episode — and it shows. Besides the lead duo's&nbsp;
inevitably impressive earnings, the show featured&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:40.020
400 shots of VFX created by a team of 100 or&nbsp;
so compositors. The sequence in which Vision&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:44.940
flies around Westview, for example, took months to&nbsp;
produce… and effects like that don't come cheap.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:48.660
Yet another entry in Marvel's Disney+ line-up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:54.240
Loki finds the God of Mischief joining the Time&nbsp;
Variance Authority to repair the damage to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:58.920
timeline caused when he swiped the Tesseract&nbsp;
in Avengers: Endgame. This wickedly fun time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:03.060
travel twister is one of the best recent&nbsp;
offerings from Marvel Studios, although,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:07.560
with a budget of about $25 million per&nbsp;
episode, it certainly wasn't cheap.

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:12.360
As you've probably guessed, Loki stars Tom&nbsp;
Hiddleston as the MCU's favorite trickster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:17.580
and, considering he was reported to have been paid&nbsp;
$8 million for his very brief role in Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:22.920
Infinity War, it's safe to say that a decent chunk&nbsp;
of the show's budget went toward his paycheck. All&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:26.760
that money at least seems to have paid off,&nbsp;
however: Many fans and critics agreed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:31.500
the series felt more like a film than a TV show,&nbsp;
and the first season was nominated for six Emmys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:35.952
including one for costumes and another&nbsp;
for outstanding production design.

00:06:35.952 --> 00:06:41.220
Perhaps unsurprisingly, The Falcon and the Winter&nbsp;
Soldier enjoyed a comparable budget to WandaVision&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:46.920
and Loki at around $25 million per episode. The&nbsp;
show takes place a few months after Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:52.020
Endgame, which ended with Sam Wilson taking&nbsp;
up Captain America's shield. Anthony Mackie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:56.460
and Sebastian Stan reprised their roles from&nbsp;
the movies, and the show didn't exactly skimp&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.460 --> 00:07:00.300
on its supporting cast, either. Not only&nbsp;
that, but The Falcon and the Winter Soldier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:05.520
was partly filmed in the Czech Republic, and&nbsp;
the COVID outbreak of 2020 completely halted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:10.200
production for several months too, likely adding&nbsp;
a significant number to the show's final cost.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:14.280
While some critics felt the show's early&nbsp;
pacing could have been better, overall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:18.240
it drew praise for its social commentary and&nbsp;
the chemistry between its leading actors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:22.620
Falcon and the Winter Soldier's budget&nbsp;
is clearly well-spent too, making it an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:27.760
enjoyable series overall — even if it isn't the&nbsp;
strongest limited series Marvel has produced.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:33.960
These days, a blockbuster movie budget is hardly&nbsp;
a rarity in the world of TV production. In 2001,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:38.520
however, it was practically unheard of.&nbsp;
Produced by Steven Spielberg and Tom Hanks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:43.020
Band of Brothers was the most expensive&nbsp;
television production to date with a budget&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:49.320
of $125 million — which would be closer to&nbsp;
$200 million today. The ten-part miniseries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:54.300
follows Easy Company, a group of World War II&nbsp;
paratroopers from the 101st Airborne Division,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:58.920
from training through their deployment on D-Day&nbsp;
and, ultimately, to the very end of the war.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:04.260
A large portion of Band of Brothers' budget went&nbsp;
to support the massive ensemble cast, many of whom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.260 --> 00:08:09.468
were relatively unknown at the time of filming but&nbsp;
have since gone on to become famous faces today.

00:08:09.766 --> 00:08:11.686
"Looks like you guys are gonna be surrounded."&nbsp;

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:15.300
"We're paratroopers, lieutenant.&nbsp;
We're supposed to be surrounded."

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:20.580
In the interest of depicting the war as accurately&nbsp;
as possible, the filmmakers and cast consulted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:25.440
many of Easy Company's surviving veterans,&nbsp;
invested in authentic uniforms and equipment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:30.480
and poured plenty of cash into realistic&nbsp;
pyrotechnics. The effort paid off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:34.680
with many World War II veterans and&nbsp;
history experts alike agreeing that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:39.008
the series presented one of the most accurate&nbsp;
portrayals of World War film ever produced.

00:08:39.008 --> 00:08:43.740
The Pacific is a 2010 production that serves&nbsp;
as a companion piece to Band of Brothers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:47.940
Much like its older sibling, The Pacific&nbsp;
became the most costly television series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:53.940
ever produced at the time of its release&nbsp;
— in total, HBO spent around $217 million.

00:08:53.940 --> 00:09:00.240
According to co-executive producer Tony To, the&nbsp;
commitment to realistically filming battle scenes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:05.700
was tremendous. Take the landing at Peleliu,&nbsp;
for example, which took four days to film and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:10.920
came in under budget at around $5 million.&nbsp;
The scene featured upwards of 300 actors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:15.420
each of whom was clad in perfectly&nbsp;
duplicated 1940s military uniforms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:20.280
that had been faithfully crafted on period looms.&nbsp;
On top of the costs of working with a large cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:26.700
producers had to factor in pricey practical&nbsp;
effects, props, and pyrotechnics, with production&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:32.940
costs coming in at around $270,000 per filming&nbsp;
day. Fortunately, producers were able to cash in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:38.576
on rebates by filming in Australia, slashing&nbsp;
the show's total cost by about $20 million.

00:09:38.576 --> 00:09:42.060
House of the Dragon is a prequel to HBO's absurdly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:46.080
successful fantasy drama series Game&nbsp;
of Thrones. And, like Game of Thrones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:50.580
House of the Dragon features an extra-large&nbsp;
ensemble cast of several dozen actors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:55.380
many of whom were already well-established&nbsp;
names when filming began. The first season's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.380 --> 00:10:01.620
budget was around $200 million, which comes out&nbsp;
to about $20 million per episode. In comparison,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:05.880
the budget for the final season of Game of&nbsp;
Thrones was around $15 million per episode.

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:10.140
Fans of George R.R. Martin will be glad to&nbsp;
know that Westeros is getting the treatment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:14.640
it deserves after cost-cutting led to some&nbsp;
not-so-flattering moments in Game of Thrones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:19.080
with Martin noting the first season's&nbsp;
small-scale jousting tournament as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:23.040
particular disappointment. Judging by the&nbsp;
incomparable tourney in House of the Dragon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:27.889
it's clear that the producers are going out of&nbsp;
their way to avoid making the same mistake twice.

00:10:27.889 --> 00:10:32.167
The first of several live-action Star&nbsp;
Wars shows to be released on Disney+,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.167 --> 00:10:36.360
The Mandalorian is a space western set&nbsp;
a few years after Return of the Jedi.

00:10:36.691 --> 00:10:37.891
"This is the way."&nbsp;

00:10:38.449 --> 00:10:41.629
"This is the way."
"This is the way."

00:10:41.629 --> 00:10:47.340
A few factors accounted for the show's price tag,&nbsp;
which equated to roughly $15 million per episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.340 --> 00:10:52.380
— not least of which was its production studio.&nbsp;
The Mandalorian was the first series to pioneer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:57.060
StageCraft technology, a type of all-around&nbsp;
AR wall that allows actors to work against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.060 --> 00:11:02.280
computer-generated backdrops. A key benefit of&nbsp;
this technology is that it creates more realistic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:07.020
lighting rather than forcing the VFX team to&nbsp;
duplicate it when working with a green screen.

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:12.540
Among the show's more surprising expenses&nbsp;
was Grogu. Rather than dump a creepy CGI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:16.680
creature into the series, producers chose&nbsp;
to go old-school Star Wars with a twist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:21.832
by investing in a foot-tall robotic puppet&nbsp;
— one that cost $5 million to build.

00:11:21.935 --> 00:11:25.980
The Book of Boba Fett is a Disney+ Star&nbsp;
Wars series that serves as a spin-off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:30.960
to The Mandalorian. The story follows the iconic&nbsp;
bounty hunter Boba Fett as he takes over Jabba the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:35.640
Hutt's criminal organization on Tatooine. While&nbsp;
the seven-episode series wasn't as well-received&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:40.380
as The Mandalorian, it came with a similar&nbsp;
price tag of around $15 million an episode.

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:44.520
While The Book of Boba Fett doesn't have&nbsp;
a multi-million dollar puppet on deck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:50.100
it does have its own costly mascot of sorts in&nbsp;
the uncannily young Luke Skywalker. Although&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:55.320
de-aging technology is improving as it becomes&nbsp;
more widely used, it remains a costly investment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.320 --> 00:12:00.060
for any production. Besides smoothing out the&nbsp;
effects of time with CGI, the show's many tech&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:05.400
experts also used an application called&nbsp;
Respeecher to rewind time on Luke's voice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:11.280
since vocal cords tend to change over time. The&nbsp;
final result? Well, the jury's out on that one.

